                <pb facs="0833" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 M Nielsen, Niels/71: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden (Myers) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-25T10:00:00+08:00">October 25, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 25—4:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Information just received from the Japanese Consulate General is to the effect
                    that Nielsen is safe at Siuyen. Details his release will be reported as soon as
                    received.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Myers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
